s city council  in 2019  and has also worked for the u.s  department of veteran affairs  there's also an open seat in the state  assembly democratic assemblyman alex  assefa has resigned  recently metro police recommended  criminal charges against decepha  in a campaign finance scandal he has not  been charged  applications to fill that seat which is  district 42 are due tuesday at noon  to be considered you have to be a  registered democrat and live in the  spring valley area here in las vegas  government investigations into ufos  we're asking the u s government to  engage in something that historically  had never wanted to engage in  up next the new timeline for the senate  to get a report on those investigations  and what's expected in the report  now you're watching  politics now the clock is ticking for  the pentagon's  hush program to investigate ufos it's  called the uap  task force and it's been ordered to  prepare a detailed overview of the ufo  mystery for submission to congress  the items george knapp has new  information about problems faced by the  task force  as a race is to meet its deadline the  first public mention of the uap  task force came in june 2020 when the  senate intelligence committee formally  asked the pentagon  for a comprehensive analysis of the ufo  mystery  over the previous three years members  and staff of key committees had received  closed-door briefings about startling  encounters between the u.s military  and unidentified aerial phenomena uaps  the senate intelligence chairman marco  rubio acknowledged to mystery wire  that lawmakers consider this to be a  serious matter this is a very simple  equation for me  there are things flying over our  military installations  we don't know what they are or where  they're they're from we don't know  some other country that's doing it and  we need to know the answer to that  question  simple in august 2020 the pentagon  formally announced the creation of the  task force  and in late december the massive bill  containing government funding and covet  relief was signed into law  as first reported by blogger danny silva  a provision in the bill  authorized the task force to prepare a  comprehensive analysis  of the ufo mystery and submit it to  congress within 180 days meaning around  june first  getting a straight story out of the  pentagon about its interest in ufos has  always been a challenge and the same is  true of the uap  task force for one thing it's not  exactly a new creation  veteran intelligence officer lou  elizondo spent years as the program  manager for atep the pentagon's previous  ufo investigation  when the new york times first revealed  the existence of atip  in december 2017 the pentagon said the  program  ended in 2012 and that it didn't really  have anything to do with ufos  neither claim was true elizondo said the  program  never ended it continued even after he  left the government  as a loose confederation of personnel in  different parts of the national security  apparatus  elements of that investigation formed  the basis of the newly named uap  task force members of the public and  media excited about the scheduled report  to congress  might want to temper their expectations  because there are significant barriers  to anything  resembling full disclosure for one thing  the report to congress will be  unclassified meaning it will not contain  the most sensitive  most classified cases or incidents  because those directly involve  national security key committees will  likely receive separate annex reports  regarding classified incidents that  information isn't likely to be made  public  secondly while the funding bill ordered  the task force to produce a  comprehensive analysis  of the uap mystery it provided no  funding  the task force was not provided with an  actual budget  only marching orders mysterywire asked  the pentagon to comment on this but  received no reply  thirdly sources familiar with the task  force say there's been a major  change at the top the high-ranking  official who's led the ufo investigation  for years  is out the name has not been made public  but we've learned it's the same official  who's been briefing congress since 2018  and who's been directly responsible for  getting elected officials  interested in the subject the navy  assigned the official to other duties  can the task force finish its job by  june 1st  maybe not it's a gigantic undertaking to  search the entire national security  system  for all relevant videos and files and  then to seek input and analysis from  other intelligence agencies  it is entirely possible the task force  will have to ask congress for more time  in a radio interview in late december  lou elizondo announced he has left to  the stars academy  the company which coaxed him into coming  forward in 2017  also departed is veteran intelligence  official chris mellon  both men say they're still supportive of  ttsa  but are now largely focused on behind  the scenes work in washington  to encourage congress and the pentagon  to move the ufo ball down the field  elizondo cautioned the public to lower  its expectations about the task force  report  saying quote this is a process not an  event we're asking the u s government to  engage in something  that historically had never wanted to  engage in i think a lot of people have  these false hopes  that disclosure is here and all of a  sudden have this huge announcement by  the u s  government progress is being made  elizondo says  the task force report will be just the  beginning he hopes congress will  authorize a permanent uap  program one that has a budget and the  authority to truly investigate  a perplexing mystery for mystery wire  george knapp  reporting now on a related note the  founder of the to the stars academy  rockstar tom de long  said they have some major ufo related  film projects that will be announced in  2020  welcome back to politics now president  joe biden says he plans to review the  trump administration's downsizing of two  national monuments here in the southwest  the boundaries redrawn in 2017 for bears  ears and the grand staircase escalante  are both in southern utah  the president says president biden he is  re-examining the monument's role  as part of his plan to fight climate  change  this week in what to watch the state of  north las vegas  mayor john lee will have his state of  the city address wednesday at 10 o'clock  in the morning  mayor lee says he will outline his idea  the horizon for the city  and coronavirus efforts it'll be  streamed on the city's facebook and  youtube pages  plus two members of the state  legislature need to uh be filled two  seats anyway by the clark county  commission  both are democratic seats we are waiting  to see who clark county will choose  to replace ivana kinsella and alex  assefa in the assembly  uh don't forget the uh legislative  session starts  on february 1st and coming up next week  here on politics now we'll take a look  at the state senate speak with lawmakers  there about what they are expecting  in the legislative session up in carson  city certainly a lot on their plate this  year  i've also watched to see in washington  dc about a possible impeachment hearing  and a trial  in the senate as well so a lot to watch  as we look ahead to next week  that's all for us this week here on  politics now thank you very much for  watching  all the political news you need is on  eight newsnow dot com  we'll see you next saturday  you
 

